{"_v":1,"id":"beetlejuice-west-end-2026","cat":"west-end","cs":65.73,"rc":9,"bd":{"positive":2,"mixed":7,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Nick Curtis","o":"Evening Standard","s":83,"b":"Rave","t":1,"u":"https://standard.co.uk/culture/theatre/beetlejuice-the-musical-review-prince-edward-b1284074.html","d":"2026-05-29","q":"Beetlejuice the musical is louche, macabre and pure, unadulterated fun, full of black-and-white grotesquerie, visual flair and near-the-knuckle jokes."},{"cn":"Alice Saville","o":"The Independent","s":62,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.independent.co.uk/arts-entertainment/theatre-dance/reviews/beetlejuice-musical-review-west-end-b2985394.html","d":"2026-05-29","q":"But this undead scene-stealer stops us from taking the actual narrative here seriously; we don’t have space to feel the aching poignancy just beneath its surface."},{"cn":"Clive Davis","o":"The Times (UK)","s":62,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.thetimes.com/culture/theatre-dance/article/beetlejuice-review-theatre-musical-tim-burton-prince-edward-london-zfgcfwq3s","d":"2026-05-29","q":"You can't help admiring a musical that tweaks the nose of the Grim Reaper quite so fearlessly."},{"cn":"Chris Wiegand","o":"The Guardian","s":60,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.theguardian.com/stage/2026/may/29/beetlejuice-the-musical-review-prince-edward-theatre-london","d":"2026-05-25","q":"All distract from the carefully designed worlds of the story."},{"cn":"Sarah Hemming","o":"Financial Times","s":59,"b":"Mixed","t":1,"u":"https://www.ft.com/content/1db58024-21e9-435a-b297-9c0ce52e588c?syn-25a6b1a6=1","d":"2026-05-29","q":"But gradually the thin yet complicated plot begins to stall and sag, and the spiky script, ingenious design and sheer gutsy energy of the cast aren’t enough to compensate."},{"cn":"Stuart King","o":"London Box Office","s":95,"b":"Rave","t":2,"q":"Tightly scripted, tightly choreographed, tightly delivered and for all that, with its great tunes it manages to feel fresh and crisply i